# Project rules: Bolt + Supabase app

- Every table gets Row Level Security with explicit policies when it's created. Users only see and change their own rows unless I say otherwise.
- Never switch or reconnect this project's database without asking first. Tell me exactly what data could be lost.
- The Supabase service_role / secret key is only used in edge functions, never in front-end code.
- Payments and calls to other services run in edge functions, with their keys stored as secrets.
- Before any schema change, list the tables and columns to add, change, or drop, and wait for my OK.
- Sign-in uses Supabase Auth. Never store passwords in our own tables.
